.TH START\-VNC\-SESSION 1 "2026-06-12" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start\-vnc\-session.sh, stop\-vnc\-session.sh, status\-vnc\-session.sh \-
manage a control room VNC session on a DAQ host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start\-vnc\-session.sh
.I session\-name display\-number
.RB [ \-g
.IR WxH ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR depth ]
.br
.B stop\-vnc\-session.sh
.I session\-name display\-number
.br
.B status\-vnc\-session.sh
.I session\-name display\-number
.RI [ name " " display " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These scripts run
.B on
a DAQ host as the session-owner account (mu2eshift, mu2edaq, mu2edcs).
They are installed to
.B ~/controlroom/bin
by
.BR install\-controlroom.sh .
.PP
.B start\-vnc\-session.sh
starts a TigerVNC server on the given display
.RB ( "vncserver \-localhost yes" ,
XFCE via
.BR ~/controlroom/etc/xstartup )
and then spawns
.B vnc\-discovery\-responder.py
\(em a sidecar that answers mu2edaq\-discovery DISCOVER queries on the
session's behalf (VNC itself has no discovery support) and multicasts a
periodic announce.
The responder PID is written to
.BR ~/.crs/vnc\-responder\-:N.pid .
Already-running displays are skipped
.RB ( SKIP ),
making the script idempotent.
.PP
.B stop\-vnc\-session.sh
kills the responder first (so the session disappears from discovery
before the port closes), then
.BR "vncserver \-kill" .
.PP
.B status\-vnc\-session.sh
prints one machine-parseable line per queried display:
.IR name|:display|port|running\:\:stopped|alive\:\:dead\:\:none .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-g " WxH"
Session geometry (default
.BR $CRS_GEOMETRY " or 1920x1080)."
.TP
.BI \-d " depth"
Color depth (default
.BR $CRS_DEPTH " or 24)."
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_HOME
Install area (default ~/controlroom).
.TP
.B CRS_ANNOUNCE_INTERVAL
Seconds between unsolicited responder announces (default 30, 0 = off).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/controlroom/log/vnc\-*.log
Per-session VNC and responder logs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crs\-remote (1),
.BR install\-controlroom (1),
.BR vncserver (1)
